		return gx.Frag(Example(ExampleProps{Item: "collapsible", Name: "collapsible-open", Label: "Collapsible: Open", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n```gx\n<collapsible.Collapsible open>\n  <:summary>Show details</:summary>\n  Hidden content.\n</collapsible.Collapsible>\n```\n\n")}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\n## Installation\n\n"), docs.Tabs(docs.TabsProps{Sync: "install", Children: gx.Frag(docs.TabItem(docs.TabItemProps{Label: "CLI", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\nRun the command in the app module.\n\n```sh frame=\"terminal\" title=\"Terminal\"\ngx add collapsible\n```\n\nThe command writes these files.\n\n| File | Path in the app |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Collapsible.gx` | `ui/collapsible/Collapsible.gx` |\n| `Collapsible.fixtures.go` | `ui/collapsible/Collapsible.fixtures.go` |\n\n")}), docs.TabItem(docs.TabItemProps{Label: "Manual", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\nCopy each file to its path in the app. Change each import of a registry package to the path of that package in the app.\n\n```gx title=\"ui/collapsible/Collapsible.gx\"\npackage collapsible\n\nprops {\n  // Summary is the content of the summary, the part that opens and closes the panel.\n  Summary  gx.Node\n  // Open renders the collapsible open. The default is closed.\n  Open     bool = false\n  // Class adds classes to the root element.\n  Class    string = \"\"\n  // Children is the content of the panel.\n  Children gx.Node\n  // Attrs adds HTML attributes to the root element.\n  Attrs    gx.Attrs = nil\n}\n\n<details open={p.Open} class={gx.Cx(\"group/collapsible [interpolate-size:allow-keywords] [&::details-content]:h-0 [&::details-content]:overflow-hidden [&::details-content]:transition-[height,content-visibility] [&::details-content]:transition-discrete [&::details-content]:duration-200 [&::details-content]:ease-out open:[&::details-content]:h-auto motion-reduce:[&::details-content]:transition-none\", p.Class)} {...p.Attrs}>\n  <summary class=\"inline-flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-2 rounded-md outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden\">{p.Summary}</summary>\n  {p.Children}\n</details>\n```\n\n```go title=\"ui/collapsible/Collapsible.fixtures.go\"\npackage collapsible\n\nimport \"github.com/alternayte/gx\"\n\nvar CollapsibleFixtures = gx.Fixtures[CollapsibleProps]{\n\t\"Open\":   {Summary: gx.Text(\"Show details\"), Open: true, Children: gx.Text(\"Hidden content.\")},\n\t\"Closed\": {Summary: gx.Text(\"Show details\"), Children: gx.Text(\"Hidden content.\")},\n}\n```\n\n")}))}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\nThe theme must define these tokens: `--ring`.\n\n## Usage\n\n```gx\n<collapsible.Collapsible summary={gx.Text(\"Show details\")}>\n  <p>Hidden content.</p>\n</collapsible.Collapsible>\n```\n\nThe panel uses the native `<details>` element.\nThe panel height animates in a browser that supports `interpolate-size`. Other browsers open the panel at once.\nThe panel has no spacing of its own. Put the spacing on the content.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Open\n\n"), Example(ExampleProps{Item: "collapsible", Name: "collapsible-open", Label: "Collapsible: Open", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n```gx\n<collapsible.Collapsible open>\n  <:summary>Show details</:summary>\n  Hidden content.\n</collapsible.Collapsible>\n```\n\n")}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\n### Closed\n\n"), Example(ExampleProps{Item: "collapsible", Name: "collapsible-closed", Label: "Collapsible: Closed", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n```gx\n<collapsible.Collapsible>\n  <:summary>Show details</:summary>\n  Hidden content.\n</collapsible.Collapsible>\n```\n\n")}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\n## API reference\n\nA tag sets a prop by its name with a lower-case first letter: `Class` is `class`.\n\n### collapsible.Collapsible\n\n| Prop | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `Summary` | `gx.Node` | Required | Summary is the content of the summary, the part that opens and closes the panel. |\n| `Open` | `bool` | `false` | Open renders the collapsible open. The default is closed. |\n| `Class` | `string` | `\"\"` | Class adds classes to the root element. |\n| `Children` | `gx.Node` | Required | Children is the content of the panel. |\n| `Attrs` | `gx.Attrs` | `nil` | Attrs adds HTML attributes to the root element. |\n\n## Do and don't\n\n"), docs.CardGrid(docs.CardGridProps{Children: gx.Frag(docs.Card(docs.CardProps{Title: "Do", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n- Use it for one optional block of content.\n- Put a verb in the summary.\n\n")}), docs.Card(docs.CardProps{Title: "Don't", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n- Do not hide essential content.\n- Do not use a collapsible for a list of questions. Use an accordion.\n\n")}))}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\n## Keyboard\n\n| Key | Action |\n| --- | --- |\n| Tab | Moves focus to the summary. |\n| Enter, Space | Opens or closes the panel. |\n"))
